<!-- snippets/product__availability.liquid -->
{% comment %}
  Availability status shown right after price: a colored dot + label
  ("IN STOCK" / "MADE TO ORDER"), with a smaller secondary line
  underneath giving the dispatch/production timeframe.

  Made-to-order is read from the selected variant's real Shopify
  inventory state (tracked, zero on hand, policy set to "continue"
  selling) - the same signal Shopify itself uses to allow adding an
  out-of-stock variant to cart. Reactive to variant switches since
  current_variant_inventory_* is already kept in sync on selection in
  assets/main-a0a73eb0.js.

  Dot color uses an inline style rather than a Tailwind utility class:
  assets/styles-816e6670.css only compiles the utility classes actually
  used elsewhere in the theme, and no bg-green-*/bg-red-* classes are
  present there, so an arbitrary color class here would silently not
  render.

  Usage:
    {% render 'product__availability' %}
{% endcomment %}

<div
  class="px-4 mb-3"
  x-show="current_variant_exists && current_variant_available && all_options_selected"
  x-cloak
>
  <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
    <span
      class="inline-block h-2 w-2 rounded-full"
      :style="(current_variant_inventory_management && current_variant_inventory_quantity <= 0 && current_variant_inventory_policy == 'continue') ? 'background-color:#8a8a8a' : 'background-color:#4caf50'"
    ></span>
    <span
      class="type--small"
      x-text="(current_variant_inventory_management && current_variant_inventory_quantity <= 0 && current_variant_inventory_policy == 'continue') ? 'MADE TO ORDER' : 'IN STOCK'"
    >
      {% comment %} No-JS fallback {% endcomment %}
      IN STOCK
    </span>
  </div>
  <div
    class="type--small opacity-75 mt-1"
    x-text="(current_variant_inventory_management && current_variant_inventory_quantity <= 0 && current_variant_inventory_policy == 'continue') ? '(production takes 10 business days, then dispatched)' : '(dispatches within 2 business days)'"
  >
    (dispatches within 2 business days)
  </div>
</div>
